Reading: at the pinned tool version, `bump-minor-pre-major` governs breaking commits and
`bump-patch-for-minor-pre-major` governs feature commits. This confirms that the binding prompt
reverses the flags and that DECISION.md corrects it accurately. `BaseStrategy.buildNewVersion`
bumps a latest release but otherwise returns `initialReleaseVersion`; Rust returns `0.1.0`; and
Manifest treats a present manifest entry as a prior released version. Those source facts, not the
TypeScript registry history, support the empty-manifest recommendation. The first real Release PR
remains explicitly unproven and assigned to P03.

